------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY / ACCEPTANCE NOTES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- States reproduced (all render, no hidden surfaces): loading (skeleton chrome),
  empty (friendly ContentUnavailableView — web `!data` branch), error (retry
  affordance), stale (stale chip + auto-refresh), offline (cached content +
  offline chip + banner), content.
- Size adaptation mirrors web exactly: compact (cols<=1) clock + optimal-start
  hero + "SOC {pct}%" + optional "${amount}/mo" success badge; standard (cols>=2)
  3 hero metric tiles (Optimal start / Target SOC / Savings/mo) + "Peak charging:
  {pct}%" + Optimized/Can-improve verdict badge + recommendation tip cards
  (maxTips 3); wide (cols>=4) adds the 24h peak/off-peak rate timeline with the
  bolt on the optimal-start hour + 5-stop axis and bumps tip cards to maxTips 5.
- DRY: reuses the existing in-module ChargingOptimizer domain model
  (OptimizerSection.Adapter.swift) rather than redefining it — both the optimizer
  feature view and this widget agree on one model. No `Mi/Mph/Kwh` legacy fields
  touched (this surface reads percentages/hours/currency only).
- Data binds via the shared P1/S8 state-holder seam (ChargingOptimizerWidgetSource
  -> ChargingOptimizerWidgetModel -> Phase); the view performs no HTTP/formatting.
  Diagnostics emit `view.opened` with slug "ChargingOptimizerWidget" on first
  appear (P1/S11), asserted once via a telemetry spy.
- Accessibility: combined VoiceOver elements per metric tile, schedule row, tip
  card and per timeline cell (web `title` tooltip "11 PM — Off-peak"), header
  refresh/open labels, a full-surface summary label + compact summary label,
  Dynamic Type via system fonts, Reduce-Motion respected.
- Tests (ChargingOptimizerWidget.Tests.swift): 33 XCTest cases = format/adapter
  parity (formatHour, fmtInt, projection, timeline, tips, verdict, guards) +
  badge-tone mapping + model phase/telemetry/wiring + registry/clamp +
  accessibility summaries. Full snapshot/UI rendering runs under the Xcode gate
  (throughput-BLOCKED here).

